    <briefdescription>
<para>GPU module configuration. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Populated at startup (from environment, YAML, or code) and validated by <ref refid="structthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_config_1a09a1f5d4dd32a5e78994dff90055abba" kindref="member">GPUConfig::validate()</ref> before the rest of the GPU module initialises. Validation failures are surfaced as a list of human-readable error strings so the caller can either abort or log all problems at once.</para>
<para>Dry-run simulation: <ref refid="structthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_config_1ac9f5a50c84ed4cb389aa386f5bf2c314" kindref="member">GPUConfig::simulateAllocation()</ref> lets operators test whether a proposed allocation would be accepted given the current config, without touching real GPU state. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
